WEBVTT

00:00:09.292 --> 00:00:10.917
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:00:10.917 --> 00:00:12.875
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:00:16.292 --> 00:00:17.875
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:00:17.875 --> 00:00:19.708
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:00:21.375 --> 00:00:23.375
<i>Shake it love, YES!</i>

00:00:23.375 --> 00:00:26.917
<i>I'm going crazy with longing</i>

00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:28.542
<i>Brushing back my hair</i>

00:00:28.542 --> 00:00:30.583
<i>That got wet in an instant</i>

00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:33.250
<i>Being toyed with by the warm rain</i>

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.750
<i>Shall I see how far I can run?</i>

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.708
<i>The prayer</i>

00:00:38.708 --> 00:00:40.708
<i>That spun out</i>

00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:43.625
<i>Connects to the future</i>

00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:44.542
<i>Overflowing</i>

00:00:44.542 --> 00:00:46.042
<i>The miracle of love</i>

00:00:46.042 --> 00:00:47.958
<i>The wonderful miracle</i>

00:00:47.958 --> 00:00:50.750
<i>The voice of these six flowers</i>

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.958
<i>is released! (Shake it love, SAY!)</i>

00:00:52.958 --> 00:00:54.792
<i>Pulling toward each other (So fast!)</i>

00:00:54.792 --> 00:00:56.458
<i>That power (So vast!)</i>

00:00:56.458 --> 00:00:58.750
<i>I want it to reach you</i>

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.042
<i>Don't stop the music</i>

00:01:00.042 --> 00:01:01.875
<i>High in the night sky (So high!)</i>

00:01:01.875 --> 00:01:03.958
<i>I send up my excitement (Turn round!)</i>

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:06.417
<i>Gravitic-romantic</i>

00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.208
<i>Tonight</i>

00:01:07.208 --> 00:01:08.875
<i>Can't be stopped (Nonstop!)</i>

00:01:08.875 --> 00:01:10.708
<i>The impulse of love (Get down!)</i>

00:01:10.708 --> 00:01:13.833
<i>I want to mess you up</i>

00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:15.542
<i>T-T-Take it easy now!</i>

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.167
<i>To embrace you</i>

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:18.833
<i>a-a-as I feel it</i>

00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:19.583
<i>Let's dance</i>

00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:22.833
<i>And once you're captivated, kiss!</i>

00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:24.583
<i>Good love! Good love!</i>

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.958
<i>Gravitic-love!</i>

00:01:26.958 --> 00:01:28.750
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.667
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:34.125
<i>Shake it love, YES!</i>

00:01:37.792 --> 00:01:42.500
"Moment of Indecision"

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.708
I'll say this first.

00:01:51.708 --> 00:01:56.625
If I'm going to do this, I'm going to be aiming
to be the best with everything I've got.

00:01:56.625 --> 00:02:00.667
Whether I'm an idol or anything else,
once I've become one, I aim for the top,

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:03.542
and what I aim for, I get.

00:02:03.542 --> 00:02:06.000
I accomplish the goals I set.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.708
At the very least, I want
Six Gravity to be a group like this.

00:02:10.708 --> 00:02:13.625
Carefree, easygoing, laid-back--

00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:15.833
I'm not interested in anything like that.

00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:18.458
If you still want to follow me,

00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:21.625
then I'll show you a good dream.

00:02:21.625 --> 00:02:23.583
I promise.

00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:26.583
Right after our group
was first brought together,

00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:29.750
before we left for our first job, Haru said,

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.250
"Let's hear from our leader,"

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:36.875
and since I hadn't prepared
anything appropriate,

00:02:36.875 --> 00:02:40.708
I just said what came to mind.

00:02:40.708 --> 00:02:45.292
I thought the members who would
follow those words were important,

00:02:45.292 --> 00:02:47.333
and as long as I was leader,

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:53.000
I would take them with me
anywhere, to any heights.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.958
That is what I vowed.

00:03:04.333 --> 00:03:06.250
It's morning already...?

00:03:11.917 --> 00:03:13.667
It's a feast!

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:16.167
It's so extravagant for breakfast!

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:19.250
It's been a long time since Yoru
and I had the same day off,

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.083
so we were a little too enthusiastic.

00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:23.125
There's <i>suimono </i>soup or Western soup,

00:03:23.125 --> 00:03:25.333
so you can choose whichever one you like.

00:03:25.333 --> 00:03:26.958
I want <i>suimono</i>, Yoru.

00:03:26.958 --> 00:03:29.583
Okay. What about you, Arata?

00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:30.917
Strawberry milk.

00:03:30.917 --> 00:03:31.708
Huh?

00:03:31.708 --> 00:03:32.833
Mornin'.

00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:34.833
Oh, something smells good.

00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:36.792
Good mornin...g.

00:03:36.792 --> 00:03:39.958
Oh? Shun isn't with you?

00:03:39.958 --> 00:03:41.417
Give me a break.

00:03:41.417 --> 00:03:45.333
I can't take on both of our
two great oversleepers myself.

00:03:48.833 --> 00:03:50.250
I see.

00:03:51.875 --> 00:03:53.917
Oh? Where are Hajime and Haru?

00:03:53.917 --> 00:03:56.917
Haru is waking Hajime up now.

00:04:00.458 --> 00:04:03.708
Morning, Hajime. Time to get up--

00:04:03.708 --> 00:04:05.000
Huh?

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.500
That's unusual. You were already awake?

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.833
Yeah.

00:04:08.833 --> 00:04:10.875
Don't tell me you didn't sleep?

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:14.750
I thought you'd been
staying up late recently, but...

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.833
I was thinking about something.

00:04:17.833 --> 00:04:19.667
Hajime, is something--

00:04:21.792 --> 00:04:24.750
Never mind. Breakfast is ready.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.292
Hurry up.

00:04:26.292 --> 00:04:27.292
Right.

00:04:34.958 --> 00:04:39.833
And so, we will start working
all-out on the joint concert

00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:42.417
between Six Gravity and Procellarum.

00:04:44.292 --> 00:04:45.167
Up until now,

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:49.125
we've been using some of your free time
for rehearsals and preparations separately,

00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:53.125
but now we will start joint rehearsals
with everyone from both groups.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:55.625
We will support you as much as we can,

00:04:55.625 --> 00:04:57.125
so let's do our best together.

00:04:57.125 --> 00:04:59.458
Whoa, it's like it's almost time.

00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:00.875
I'm getting excited!

00:05:00.875 --> 00:05:04.292
Don't get so excited that
you fall during the concert.

00:05:04.292 --> 00:05:07.750
Yeah, can't crash into the ceiling
and be completely turned upside-down--

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.167
Wait, Arata!

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:10.833
Don't say such unlucky things!

00:05:10.833 --> 00:05:12.542
Now, now.

00:05:12.542 --> 00:05:15.458
It's like this day has finally come.

00:05:15.458 --> 00:05:20.167
We've always said we wanted to have a
joint concert one day, ever since we first started.

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:23.667
Let's make sure we have
a great performance! Right, Rui?

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:25.875
Yeah, I'll do my best.

00:05:30.833 --> 00:05:33.458
Is something the matter, Hajime?

00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:36.583
No, things are going well, huh?

00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:37.542
Of course.

00:05:37.542 --> 00:05:39.250
Everything's going well.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:43.042
This must also be thanks
to everyone working hard

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:45.958
under the leadership of our
charismatic leader, the great Hajime.

00:05:45.958 --> 00:05:48.542
You're amazing, King.

00:05:57.958 --> 00:05:59.375
Thanks for the food.

00:06:00.917 --> 00:06:02.375
You're done already?

00:06:02.375 --> 00:06:04.417
Oh, how about some after-breakfast coffee?

00:06:04.417 --> 00:06:05.375
No, thanks.

00:06:05.375 --> 00:06:08.125
If I don't leave soon, I'll be late for work.

00:06:08.125 --> 00:06:10.042
I see...

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:19.417
It was delicious. Sorry for not finishing it.

00:06:19.417 --> 00:06:20.792
Oh, it's all right...

00:06:20.792 --> 00:06:22.250
Have a nice day...

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:25.042
Oh, have a nice day!

00:06:25.042 --> 00:06:28.250
Was Hajime the only one
who couldn't get today off?

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:32.125
He's working too much.
He has a lot of jobs by himself, too.

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:35.000
I wonder if he's okay... I hope
he's not pushing himself too much.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:40.167
Don't worry, Aoi. Can you
imagine that guy exhausted?

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:41.583
Huh?

00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:44.250
Not at all.

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:51.500
Hajime is really reliable and kind,
like an absolute leader.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.667
Those of us in Procella respect him, too.

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:57.500
Our leader's just unique.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:02.042
Do you think there's another group as worried
about their leader doing something weird

00:07:02.042 --> 00:07:03.458
as we are?

00:07:03.458 --> 00:07:07.208
Um... what to do? I can't deny it completely.

00:07:10.208 --> 00:07:16.042
Even our absolute leader seems like
he's worried about something, though.

00:07:16.042 --> 00:07:17.625
Hajime's worried?

00:07:17.625 --> 00:07:21.000
Are pigs going to fly?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.417
Hey, Kai, just what do you think
our Hajime is, anyway?

00:07:26.958 --> 00:07:29.792
Sorry, it was a joke.

00:07:29.792 --> 00:07:31.583
But it's unexpected.

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:37.208
Even if he does have worries, it's not
like him to allow us to figure that out.

00:07:37.208 --> 00:07:39.125
He won't talk to you about it?

00:07:41.042 --> 00:07:46.292
I think it's not something he can ask for
advice about just because we're friends.

00:07:46.292 --> 00:07:48.000
Just a feeling.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:54.292
All right! Then what about this?

00:07:54.292 --> 00:07:57.167
Let's see... "Set a thief to catch a thief"!

00:07:57.167 --> 00:07:58.958
Wait, is that right?

00:08:52.875 --> 00:08:54.917
Oh, that's good.

00:08:54.917 --> 00:08:57.500
Should I shift my gaze a little?

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:01.667
If you go overboard, the girls will scream.

00:09:03.083 --> 00:09:04.792
"Bringing the radiance of the moon to you"
This is unconventional, though.

00:09:04.792 --> 00:09:08.000
To have a male idol for a cosmetics commercial.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:12.583
But people really seem to like it, so I'm sure
you'll get more and more fans.

00:09:12.583 --> 00:09:16.375
I'm sure your upcoming concert
will be a big success, too.

00:09:17.875 --> 00:09:20.292
I hope that is the case.

00:09:21.292 --> 00:09:23.000
I don't expect any less from you.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.458
Okay, that's a wrap!

00:09:25.458 --> 00:09:27.000
Good work today!

00:09:39.625 --> 00:09:41.125
Mr. Tsukishiro?

00:09:41.125 --> 00:09:44.292
I just finished. About the meeting--

00:09:46.292 --> 00:09:49.833
I see. Then, I will go straight home today.

00:09:49.833 --> 00:09:51.292
Thanks.

00:09:59.333 --> 00:10:02.750
Have you started waiting for me
to come out now, Shun?

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:08.208
That sounds fun, too, but today,
I came to ask you out on a date.

00:10:08.208 --> 00:10:09.417
Huh?

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:30.000
--Richer, deeper, sweeter...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.125
--Hajime's in another commercial.
--Richer, deeper, sweeter...

00:10:33.125 --> 00:10:34.625
Here, Rui. Tea.

00:10:34.625 --> 00:10:35.208
--Have a piece, Miss.

00:10:35.208 --> 00:10:37.208
--Thanks.
--Have a piece, Miss.

00:10:37.208 --> 00:10:39.083
Here, for you too, Aoi.

00:10:39.083 --> 00:10:41.542
Thanks, Yoru.

00:10:41.542 --> 00:10:43.125
Strawberry milk for you, Arata...

00:10:43.125 --> 00:10:45.542
Oh, he's sleeping.

00:10:45.542 --> 00:10:48.375
Oh, is it already this late?

00:10:48.375 --> 00:10:50.750
Maybe I'll start getting dinner ready soon.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.708
What, are you making dinner, Aoi?

00:10:53.708 --> 00:10:57.000
I was resting while Hajime was working,

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:00.083
so I thought at least I can make
something delicious for him to eat...

00:11:00.083 --> 00:11:02.750
That sounds good. I'll help, too!

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:04.500
Thanks.

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:08.208
Speaking of Hajime, don't you think
it's kind of late for him to still be out?

00:11:08.208 --> 00:11:10.750
Oh yeah, he's been out since morning.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:13.833
He should be back by now.

00:11:13.833 --> 00:11:16.792
What if he got so tired he
passed out exhausted somewhere?

00:11:16.792 --> 00:11:20.083
Arata, don't say something scary out of the blue.

00:11:20.083 --> 00:11:22.417
I was kidding.

00:11:22.417 --> 00:11:27.583
But it's true that Hajime seems to be
working a little too much lately...

00:11:27.583 --> 00:11:31.792
Well, it wouldn't be strange for a normal
human to have passed out by now.

00:11:31.792 --> 00:11:35.167
Don't say that. He's still young.

00:11:35.167 --> 00:11:36.958
Young people who work too much?

00:11:36.958 --> 00:11:41.625
Yes, recently, there has been a problem
with young people who work too much.

00:11:41.625 --> 00:11:43.583
"Special: Overwork of young people!?"
You should pay close attention if they suddenly

00:11:43.583 --> 00:11:47.625
"Special: Overwork of young people!?"
lose their appetite, or sigh for no reason.

00:11:47.625 --> 00:11:49.375
Now that I think about it,

00:11:49.375 --> 00:11:53.667
don't you think Hajime's been sighing a lot
recently with a brooding look on his face?

00:11:53.667 --> 00:11:56.875
He barely touched his breakfast.

00:11:58.375 --> 00:12:02.375
K-Kakeru, what work did Hajime have today?

00:12:02.375 --> 00:12:05.708
I don't think he had anything too strenuous.

00:12:05.708 --> 00:12:10.375
Let's see... I think he said he'd be promoting
something on a variety show around noon.

00:12:16.875 --> 00:12:20.208
Then filming a commercial for
women's cosmetics in the afternoon.

00:12:20.208 --> 00:12:21.625
Cosmetics...

00:12:23.458 --> 00:12:26.042
Oh, that's a cleanser!

00:12:29.667 --> 00:12:34.625
And Mr. Tsukishiro had something come up
today, so he doesn't have anyone with him.

00:12:34.625 --> 00:12:36.292
No one with him...?

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:43.417
Hajime...!

00:12:43.417 --> 00:12:45.333
Wait, wait! Hey!

00:12:45.333 --> 00:12:47.958
It's getting blown out of proportion.

00:12:47.958 --> 00:12:52.458
Yeah. It's Hajime, so we don't have to worry.

00:12:52.458 --> 00:12:53.875
Calm down, everyone.

00:12:55.208 --> 00:12:56.250
Yeah, <i>y</i>ou should.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.167
Arata...

00:12:58.167 --> 00:13:00.917
Everyone, let's calm dow--

00:13:02.083 --> 00:13:03.583
The cup...

00:13:07.042 --> 00:13:09.625
The cup broke by itself!

00:13:09.625 --> 00:13:12.208
And an unlucky black cat...

00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:15.458
And an unlucky black rabbit...

00:13:15.458 --> 00:13:18.875
No, the black cat and
black rabbit are always here.

00:13:18.875 --> 00:13:20.042
Ha...

00:13:20.042 --> 00:13:22.917
Hajime...!

00:13:25.375 --> 00:13:27.458
I thought you were joking.

00:13:27.458 --> 00:13:31.042
I didn't think you'd actually
bring me to a date spot.

00:13:31.042 --> 00:13:35.208
What are two guys like us doing here?

00:13:35.208 --> 00:13:41.000
Well, there's a reason why people
gather in the places they do.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:46.708
A typical date spot means it's
like a "power spot" for couples.

00:13:46.708 --> 00:13:52.250
I'll grasp at any straws to fulfill my
long-standing affection for you, Hajime.

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.458
I'm going to pretend you didn't say that.

00:13:54.458 --> 00:14:02.125
Anyway, I was traveling by taxi today, so
I don't have a hat or glasses to disguise myself.

00:14:02.125 --> 00:14:03.958
Don't worry.

00:14:05.875 --> 00:14:07.500
Isn't it strange?

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:12.333
Even though there are so many people here,
no one is paying any attention to us.

00:14:12.333 --> 00:14:18.542
It means that right now, we're completely
blending in with the regular people.

00:14:18.542 --> 00:14:22.583
Shun, did you do something?

00:14:22.583 --> 00:14:26.208
Just a special little charm.

00:14:26.208 --> 00:14:27.875
Do you feel better now?

00:14:27.875 --> 00:14:32.417
With this, we can have a fun-filled date without
worrying about other people looking at us.

00:14:32.417 --> 00:14:34.292
Come on, let's go!

00:14:36.792 --> 00:14:40.750
Recently, I've been thinking back
to when we first debuted.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:42.750
When you first debuted?

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:46.917
Back then, no one knew who we were.

00:14:46.917 --> 00:14:52.958
It was true that we were idols,
but society didn't pay any attention to us.

00:14:52.958 --> 00:14:56.000
It's not like that wasn't frustrating,

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.917
but I kind of liked that feeling.

00:15:05.458 --> 00:15:07.542
"We're at zero right now.

00:15:07.542 --> 00:15:12.583
It's up to us whether we
make it to ten or a hundred."

00:15:12.583 --> 00:15:15.208
Thinking about it like that
made me feel excited, like a kid.

00:15:15.208 --> 00:15:19.125
It made me feel like
whatever I did was worth doing.

00:15:19.125 --> 00:15:21.000
Is it different now?

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:28.500
Having a big joint concert with Gravi
and Procella has always been my dream.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:34.000
Isn't it amazing that I can
accomplish my goal so soon?

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:38.625
All the members are happy about it,
and the staff have all been enthusiastic.

00:15:38.625 --> 00:15:43.875
In the midst of that, I am the only one
who hadn't quite processed the situation.

00:15:45.208 --> 00:15:49.958
Thinking, "Oh, dreams can come true so easily."

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:56.208
You know that some people spend their whole lives
trying to make their dreams come true, right?

00:15:56.208 --> 00:16:00.542
I know. I know that it's
a luxury to worry about this.

00:16:00.542 --> 00:16:07.625
But... it's like I suddenly received
a reward in the middle of my journey...

00:16:07.625 --> 00:16:09.458
That's what it feels like.

00:16:11.208 --> 00:16:13.625
You're really...

00:16:16.583 --> 00:16:18.833
It's getting late.

00:16:18.833 --> 00:16:20.875
Let's go somewhere else.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.583
You wanted to come here?

00:16:28.583 --> 00:16:30.458
Why did we come to a place like this?

00:16:33.417 --> 00:16:34.375
"Finally"

00:16:35.167 --> 00:16:35.542
"they will--"

00:16:40.292 --> 00:16:41.542
Look, look!

00:16:41.542 --> 00:16:43.042
No way, I love them!

00:16:43.042 --> 00:16:44.625
They're so cool!

00:16:46.417 --> 00:16:49.083
Did you do this?

00:16:50.375 --> 00:16:52.958
What are you, really?

00:16:52.958 --> 00:16:55.500
Did you hijack the airwaves?

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:57.167
Forget about that.

00:16:57.167 --> 00:16:58.958
<i>Que sera sera</i>.

00:16:58.958 --> 00:17:01.083
It's a little demon world secret.

00:17:03.167 --> 00:17:04.333
Well?

00:17:04.333 --> 00:17:08.000
There are so many people
who are happy about this,

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.250
so why are you still looking so unsatisfied?

00:17:13.917 --> 00:17:20.458
Our Rui said before that we're still
in the middle of our dreams.

00:17:21.667 --> 00:17:28.500
As long as we believe that, those girls
can continue to dream in the same way.

00:17:29.542 --> 00:17:34.625
That's right. To these girls, the joint
live isn't the end of the dream.

00:17:34.625 --> 00:17:40.042
Their dream still continues
as long as we are shining.

00:17:41.333 --> 00:17:46.708
That's why you just have to
shine brighter than you are now.

00:17:46.708 --> 00:17:51.208
It's a waste if you decide on
your own that the dream is over.

00:17:51.208 --> 00:17:53.083
Stretch out your hand more.

00:17:53.083 --> 00:17:54.875
Be greedier.

00:17:54.875 --> 00:17:56.917
Be more ambitious.

00:17:56.917 --> 00:17:59.833
I like you like that.

00:17:59.833 --> 00:18:02.708
And I'm a little jealous, too.

00:18:03.792 --> 00:18:05.208
Shun...

00:18:07.083 --> 00:18:08.875
Oh my.

00:18:08.875 --> 00:18:12.375
I love boring days more than anything.

00:18:12.375 --> 00:18:15.500
Can you refrain from making me
say things that aren't like me?

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.208
I'm tired now.

00:18:20.167 --> 00:18:24.333
You're right. It's still too soon
to feel like we've reached our goal.

00:18:24.333 --> 00:18:26.750
There are still things that I--

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.542
that <i>w</i>e--can do.

00:18:29.542 --> 00:18:32.625
If you'll let me say one more thing...

00:18:33.958 --> 00:18:38.708
At least at times like this,
you should talk to someone about it.

00:18:38.708 --> 00:18:42.458
You're strict with yourself,
an idealist and a perfectionist.

00:18:42.458 --> 00:18:46.000
You tend to take everything onto yourself.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.792
I mean, that's part of
what's cool about you, though.

00:18:48.792 --> 00:18:50.542
Are you teasing me?

00:18:52.125 --> 00:18:58.125
But you know, kings don't have to
do everything by themselves.

00:18:58.125 --> 00:19:03.792
I'm the one who pushes all my servants--I mean,
friends--around in Procella Kingdom,

00:19:03.792 --> 00:19:07.667
and I'm saying it, so you know it's true.

00:19:07.667 --> 00:19:09.333
You...

00:19:09.333 --> 00:19:15.667
From now on, don't you think you can take
more advantage of the people who love you?

00:19:15.667 --> 00:19:17.083
King.

00:19:18.333 --> 00:19:21.000
Yeah. I'll think about it.

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:27.042
Now, I think our ride's about here.

00:19:27.042 --> 00:19:28.458
Ride?

00:19:44.542 --> 00:19:47.083
Oh, they're both asleep.

00:19:47.083 --> 00:19:50.917
I understand about Hajime,
but why is Shun sleeping, too?

00:19:50.917 --> 00:19:55.250
Maybe because Shun was being
considerate of Hajime in his own way?

00:19:55.250 --> 00:20:00.042
I see. The demon king is tired from
doing things he's not used to, huh?

00:20:01.667 --> 00:20:04.667
It looks like he's moved forward
in a good direction, huh?

00:20:04.667 --> 00:20:07.583
Maybe it was right to leave it to Shun.

00:20:07.583 --> 00:20:13.667
Don't carelessly say things
that'll make this guy happy like that.

00:20:13.667 --> 00:20:15.958
Oh? You were awake?

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:17.708
Wh--?!

00:20:17.708 --> 00:20:19.125
Did you hear that, Hajime?

00:20:19.125 --> 00:20:21.042
Your partner's given his stamp of approval.

00:20:21.042 --> 00:20:23.792
I'm officially a friend
recognized by Haru from today.

00:20:23.792 --> 00:20:25.375
Go back to sleep.

00:20:34.208 --> 00:20:35.375
Hajime!

00:20:35.375 --> 00:20:37.292
Hajime! You're okay?!

00:20:37.292 --> 00:20:39.958
Welcome home!

00:20:39.958 --> 00:20:42.667
Y-Yeah... I'm back.

00:20:42.667 --> 00:20:47.125
Anyway, why are you all here?

00:20:47.125 --> 00:20:51.208
We were all worried since you came home late.

00:20:51.208 --> 00:20:54.833
What, you were hanging out
with Kai and the others?

00:20:54.833 --> 00:20:56.958
I shouldn't've worried.

00:20:56.958 --> 00:21:00.333
But I'm glad you weren't in an accident.

00:21:00.333 --> 00:21:01.875
You're overreacting.

00:21:06.375 --> 00:21:09.250
Sorry to make you worry.

00:21:12.333 --> 00:21:14.792
Hajime, the bath's ready.

00:21:14.792 --> 00:21:16.583
You should get some sleep today--

00:21:26.917 --> 00:21:29.417
You look happy.

00:21:34.875 --> 00:21:37.208
Good night, King.

00:21:37.208 --> 00:21:38.625
Sweet dreams.

00:22:06.583 --> 00:22:11.792
<i>Stretching straight out as far as I can</i>

00:22:11.792 --> 00:22:22.125
<i>Excited thoughts on the other side</i>
<i>of the unending horizon</i>

00:22:22.125 --> 00:22:28.083
<i>I won't forget them for a second</i>

00:22:28.083 --> 00:22:31.792
<i>Even if I fall seven times</i>

00:22:33.375 --> 00:22:38.875
<i>I'll get up eight times</i>

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:41.417
<i>"Never Ending Challenge!!"</i>

00:22:41.417 --> 00:22:43.167
<i>Far away in the distance</i>

00:22:43.167 --> 00:22:45.917
<i>I gaze at the white tape</i>

00:22:45.917 --> 00:22:48.417
<i>Never taking my eyes off it</i>

00:22:48.417 --> 00:22:51.125
<i>I just have to run through it</i>

00:22:51.125 --> 00:22:53.792
<i>Renewing my vow right now</i>

00:22:53.792 --> 00:22:56.708
<i>It's been my dream ever since I was young</i>

00:22:56.708 --> 00:23:01.833
<i>Feeling the wind in the blue heights</i>

00:23:01.833 --> 00:23:03.083
<i>Make a wish! </i>

00:23:13.542 --> 00:23:17.292
I'm Procellarum's manager, Dai Kurotsuki.

00:23:17.292 --> 00:23:22.083
We've started going all out on the preparations
for the Gravi and Procella joint concert.

00:23:22.083 --> 00:23:24.750
All the members are also really into it!

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.250
It looks like there's a lot they want to do, too.

00:23:28.333 --> 00:23:31.167
Next time, "Full Moon Festival."

00:23:31.167 --> 00:23:33.625
There's not much time until the concert!

00:23:33.625 --> 00:23:36.833
Everyone, please watch over them!

00:23:36.833 --> 00:23:42.059
Tsukishiro, we need to support them
with everything we've got, too!
